{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=y\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+2y,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(8,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-32662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2y+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{y}-y+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{y}-y+2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(8,4),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(8,4)} & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{4}-4+2)}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-32662" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ca32cba778c0497fdefe3b318aaf2c1ab28076f1609d8e4c3cfe388d73b4036"} {"question" "q-32662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-32662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-32662" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=y+\\frac{3}{{y}^{3}},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+\\frac{3}{{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =1+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{-4}) \\\\  & =1-9{y}^{-4} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{9}{{y}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{4}-9}{{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{4}}{{y}^{4}-9}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{4}}{{1}^{4}-9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-4) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ca32cba778c0497fdefe3b318aaf2c1ab28076f1609d8e4c3cfe388d73b4036"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-10x+44"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{10}+\\frac{7}{5}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{33}{8}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{{y}^{3}})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}-2{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{1/2}}{2}-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{7/2}-4}{2{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3{y}^{7/2}-4}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1)^{3}}{3(1)^{7/2}-4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-2(x-2) \\\\ y & =-2x+4+1 \\\\ y & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ca32cba778c0497fdefe3b318aaf2c1ab28076f1609d8e4c3cfe388d73b4036"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2x+2"] ["math" "y=-2x+4"] ["math" "y=-2x+5"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{3}{4}x+\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-170191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-2x+5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-341745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x={y}^{4}-\\frac{3}{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(4,-1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,-1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-341745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{4}-\\frac{3}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{4})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}-3(-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}+3{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =4{y}^{3}+\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{5}+3}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4{y}^{5}+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(4,-1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,-1)} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{4(-1)^{5}+3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-341745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ca32cba778c0497fdefe3b318aaf2c1ab28076f1609d8e4c3cfe388d73b4036"} {"question" "q-341745" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-341745" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-342061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=6\\sqrt{y}-2{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-342061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(6\\sqrt{y}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-2(2y) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-4y \\\\  & =3{y}^{-1/2}-4y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}-4y \\\\  & =\\frac{3-4y\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{3-4y\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}}{3-4(1)\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-(x-4) \\\\ y & =-x+4+1 \\\\ y & =-x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-342061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2ca32cba778c0497fdefe3b318aaf2c1ab28076f1609d8e4c3cfe388d73b4036"} {"question" "q-342061" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"} {"question" "q-342061" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x+5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981557/state.json" "file_sha256" "3233be5fe1edf007ef710bae3c41fe87305df15c7c8252099b609c2db15533d7"}] "usage" {} "basis" 895 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
